From 84ae673405bbeb1411633f9538d36bba6cfc0455 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caio Oliveira <caio.oliveira@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:35:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] jay: Handle uniform derivatives without varying temporaries

If a derivative source was identified as uniform, emit `x - x`
directly (which preserves NaN and infinity behavior).  This
fixes jay validation failure in Oblivion fossil:

The failing sequence was:

```text
   u2009 = mov.u32 u53
   r3291 = quad_swizzle.u32 u2009, xxxx
   r3292 = quad_swizzle.u32 u2009, yyyy
   u2010 = add.f32 r3292, -r3291
```

Original error:

```text
  jay shader validation failed (after NIR->Jay translation):
     invalid instruction in block 45: u2010 = add.f32 r3292, -r3291
     assertion failed at ../src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_validate.c:212
     def.file != GPR || jay_is_null(def) || jay_simd_width_logical(validate->func->shader, I) > 1 || I->op ==
JAY_OPCODE_SHUFFLE || I->op == JAY_OPCODE_MOV_INDIRECT || I->op == JAY_OPCODE_BROADCAST_IMM
```

Assisted-by: LLM
Fixes: b768fe8188bb ("jay: set nir_divergence_single_prim_per_subgroup")
Reviewed-by: Kenneth Graunke <kenneth@whitecape.org>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45634>
---
 src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_from_nir.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_from_nir.c b/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_from_nir.c
index 204f1472e228..d8e0ee2116ba 100644
--- a/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_from_nir.c
+++ b/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_from_nir.c
@@ -1036,6 +1036,12 @@ jay_emit_derivative(jay_builder *b,
    assert(intr->def.bit_size == 32 && "todo");
    jay_def val = nj_src(intr->src[0]);
 
+   /* Keep x - x for NaNs and Infs. */
+   if (jay_is_uniform(val)) {
+      jay_ADD(b, JAY_TYPE_F32, dst, val, jay_negate(val));
+      return;
+   }
+
    /* dFdyfine gets split down to SIMD4 which requires UGPR vector temporaries
     * for correctness (to get NoMask in non-uniform control flow).
     */
